      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): preserve surrogate pairs when truncating LLM text in bench dump",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`scripts/repro/tool-surface-live-bench.ts` uses `String.prototype.slice(0, N)` at three sites to truncate LLM output text for benchmark trail/log output. `slice` operates on UTF-16 code units, so when a surrogate pair (emoji, CJK character) straddles the cut boundary at position 299-300 or 399-400, the result contains an unpaired high surrogate — invalid Unicode that downstream consumers may reject.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace with `truncateUtf16Safe` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice`, the same helper already used across the codebase for safe UTF-16 boundary truncation (e.g. openai-completions `normalizeToolCallId`, PR #110471). Sibling UTF-16 PRs (#104054, #107664, #109561, #109498, #109839) all use the same helper.\n\nCollision check: searched open PRs for `tool-surface-live-bench`, `truncateUtf16Safe`, `bench dump`; no same-file or same-problem open PR was found.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBenchmark trail and result dump output no longer produces invalid Unicode. No production impact — this file is a `scripts/repro/` bench tool.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `57172587d24a7cf8a8f86d82c34804bc3729cbd8`\n\n`oxfmt --check scripts/repro/tool-surface-live-bench.ts test/scripts/tool-surface-live-bench.test.ts` — passed.\n`git diff --check` — passed; exit 0.\n\n### Tests\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/tool-surface-live-bench.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  8 passed (8)\n   Start at  16:57:54\n   Duration  6.80s\n```\n\nTest coverage across all 3 truncation call sites:\n\n- **Site 1 (L693)** `ASSISTANT text: ${truncateUtf16Safe(text, 300)}` — surrogate at 299-300 stripped cleanly; ASCII path identical to slice\n- **Site 2 (L698)** `TOOLRESULT ${name}: ${truncateUtf16Safe(content, 400)}` — surrogate at 399-400 stripped cleanly; ASCII path identical to slice\n- **Site 3 (L730)** `finalText: truncateUtf16Safe(finalText, 400)` — surrogate at 399-400 stripped cleanly; JSON round-trip valid\n- **Import verified** — `truncateUtf16Safe` imported from the same module used by the bench script\n\n### Mutation checks\n\n- Revert `truncateUtf16Safe` → `.slice()` at each of the 3 call sites → tests FAIL: `hasTrailingSurrogate` returns true. Restore → 8/8 passed.\n- ASCII paths (`truncateUtf16Safe` matches `.slice()`) pass with and without the fix, proving no regression.\n\n### Not tested\n\n- Live benchmark run requiring LLM API keys (output construction tested via the exact same production helper, boundary lengths, and format strings used by the bench script)",
